        "original_id": "c81d07ab-6240-5a50-a58d-15918e5884b0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Glide Path\n- People: Arthur C. Clarke\n- Organizations: Royal Air Force\n- Projects: GCA project\n- Concepts: aerial warfare force, independent air force\n\nFacts:\n- The Royal Air Force was formed on 1 April 1918 toward the end of the First World War.\n- The Royal Air Force is the United Kingdom's aerial warfare force.\n- The Royal Air Force is the oldest independent air force in the world.\n- Arthur C. Clarke published the novel Glide Path in 1963.\n- Glide Path is based on Arthur C. Clarke's wartime service with the Royal Air Force.\n- During Arthur C. Clarke's wartime service with the Royal Air Force, he worked on the GCA project.",
